#
# Well-formed: a derivative naming what it differentiates, its variable, and its
# order — and, as a math:BindingExpression, the math:VariableDeclaration it binds
# and its body through an indexed math:argumentSlot. Conforms to
# math:DerivativeShape and math:BindingExpressionShape. Bound by ex:ecDerivativeFramed.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:velocity a math:Derivative ;
    math:operator math:differentiationBinder ;
    math:derivativeOf ex:positionFn ;
    math:withRespectToVariable ex:timeDecl ;
    math:derivativeOrder 1 ;
    math:boundVariable ex:timeDecl ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:velocitySlot0 .

ex:velocitySlot0 a math:ArgumentSlot ;
    math:slotIndex 0 ;
    math:slotExpression ex:positionFn .

# The differentiated function is named, not decomposed: a math:SymbolReference resolving to a
# SYMBOL is the concrete form for that. The abstract math:MathematicalExpression base names no
# form and carries no structural identity (math:UnrecognizedExpressionType).
ex:positionFn a math:SymbolReference ; math:hasMathematicalSymbol ex:positionFnSymbol .
ex:positionFnSymbol a math:MathematicalSymbol .
ex:timeDecl a math:VariableDeclaration .
